61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Looking at the options, Corvus is too modular, which we've agreed is a risk. Tessera relies on a partner for training, which might not stick. Anchor is on-premise, risking the stagnation Benjamin mentioned. I lean toward Meridian.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, I agree about Corvus. Anchor sounds good because they're on-site, but if it's just for the rollout, we're stuck later. Meridian's hosted suite seems safer for our old gear and peak season. I'll go with Meridian.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Corvus is out; separate licenses are exactly the financial trap I feared. Anchor's on-premise model risks the same neglect Benjamin noted. Meridian's hosted suite and fixed configuration offer the price stability and unity we need. I vote Meridian.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, @Kenji, @Misaki, I'm with you! Meridian is a hosted suite, so it's one package and one team. That's way better than the finger-pointing we had before! I vote Meridian!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is inescapable. Corvus is a financial minefield, and Anchor risks the same on-premise decay we have already suffered. Tessera's reliance on a third party for migration is too risky. Meridian is the only rational choice. I vote Meridian.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Since we are all in agreement and have each cast our votes for Meridian Systems, I believe our decision is clear. It is the most stable choice for our staff and our budget.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
67,3,2,pass,Misaki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm totally happy with this! Meridian seems like the best way to make sure the depot keeps moving without any more disasters. I'm all in.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
69,3,2,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
70,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Meridian provides the bundled structure and accountability we require to avoid both financial surprises and operational gaps. My vote remains with Meridian.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
71,3,2,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
72,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm so glad we all agree! Meridian is definitely the way to go to keep things simple and happy for everyone. I'm sticking with my vote for Meridian!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
